=== Regional Variation and Moveable Dates

Three practical caveats apply to the table above. First, German holidays are partly regional: several observances apply only in certain federal states, and the Berlin, Munich, and Cologne offices do not always close together. Second, moveable feasts drift against the civil calendar from year to year, so a holiday encountered in March one year may fall in April the next. Third, substitute days: when a statutory holiday lands on an ordinary rest day, jurisdictions differ on whether and when a substitute day is observed. The Travel Desk maintains a short consolidation memo each January covering all three points; reading it before booking January travel is a small investment with a reliable return.

